            "en": "A synchronous listener exception may propagate back to the publisher. An asynchronous executor can be configured, but context, failures, and backpressure then require explicit handling. `@TransactionalEventListener` can bind execution to a transaction phase such as after commit, but a crash after commit and before an external side effect still loses work. Reliable cross-system events need a durable design such as an outbox."
